<title>USA: Vimpel-Communications IPO price range increased.</title>
<headline>Vimpel-Communications IPO price range increased.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lead underwriter Donaldson Lufkin Jenrette said on Thursday that the price range for the initial public offering of Vimpel-Communications had been increased to $19.50 to $20.50, from $15.75 to $18.75 a share.</p>
<p>Vimpel-Communications, the largest cellular telecommunications provider in Russia, is expected to make its market debut Friday on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol &quot;VIP&quot;, DLJ said.</p>
</text>
